# Architecture Analysis Rule

Always analyze existing architecture before implementing features.

## Required Steps
1. Search the codebase for similar functionality (use `codebase_search`).
2. Read related components to learn current patterns.
3. Identify existing state management and data flow.
4. Check existing UI patterns and component hierarchies.

## Checklist Before Implementation
- [ ] No duplicate functionality
- [ ] Existing patterns followed
- [ ] Existing state management used
- [ ] Existing UI patterns respected
- [ ] Existing APIs leveraged

## Red Flags
- Creating new state management when existing stores work
- Duplicating UI components similar to existing ones
- Placing functionality in the wrong location (e.g., header vs sidebar)
- Ignoring existing component hierarchies

Goal: Enhance what exists; do not replace it.